    {
      "id": "4gcrqaw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Latitudes"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Latitudes and Longitudes define geographical locations and coordinates across the globe.",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is derived from a specific reference longitude passing through India.",
        "The Tropic of Cancer passes through specific designated Indian states.",
        "The Equator serves as the primary line of latitude, crossing multiple continents and countries.",
        "Understanding the comparison between Latitudes and Longitudes is fundamental for time zone and location calculations."
      ],
      "id": "qs5oh8m"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m0tvn1m",
      "content": "• Latitudes are imaginary lines drawn parallel to the Equator. "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vzq0s4u",
      "content": "• They measure distance north or south of the Equator."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l3cd4y3",
      "content": "• The Equator is 0° latitude."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kkbjbq7",
      "content": "• Latitudes extend from 0° to 90° North and 0° to 90° South."
    },
    {
      "id": "su3okyc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Important Latitudes"
    },
    {
